# Day 08 - Arrays: Reverse Array

## Problem Statement

Given an array of integers, print the elements in reverse order.

## Example

Input:

```text
4
1 4 3 2
```

Output:

```text
2 3 4 1
```

## Approach

1. Read the size of the array `n`.
2. Read all array elements into a list.
3. Traverse the array from the last index to the first index.
4. Print each element while maintaining proper spacing.

## Concepts Used

* Arrays / Lists
* Loops
* Input Handling
* Reverse Traversal
* Java Streams

## Code Logic

```java
for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    System.out.print(arr.get(i));

    if (i > 0) {
        System.out.print(" ");
    }
}
```

The loop starts from the last element and moves backward until the first element, printing the array in reverse order.

## Time Complexity

* O(n)

## Space Complexity

* O(n)

